ICEWS DATA AND DERIVED-RESULTS NOTICE
======================================

This repository contains source code and aggregate results. It does not contain
an ICEWS event table, a local data directory, row-level predictions or labels.

Source data
-----------
The results are derived from the Integrated Crisis Early Warning System (ICEWS)
event data, doi:10.7910/DVN/28075, version 37.0, published by the Harvard
Dataverse. ICEWS is made available for research and teaching purposes only.
Redistribution of the event data is not permitted.

The public tree therefore excludes raw and derived event panels, parquet files,
feature caches, run logs and row-level predictions/labels. Do not add such files
to a public repository or mirror.

Derived aggregate results
-------------------------
The `results/` tree includes aggregate quantities computed from ICEWS, for
example model metrics and confidence intervals, actor-level aggregate
attribution and exposure tables, top-actor lists, transition counts, and a
rendered world-line illustration with per-anchor aggregate tallies. Actor-level
predicted probabilities (`mean_p`, `p_sum`) and observed outcome counts/rates
(`y_sum`, `mean_y`) are not released, and the world-line preview ships no
row-level trace or per-row probability file. These are small-sample or
aggregate research outputs; they do not permit reconstruction of the event
panel and must not be used to attempt re-identification. The exact removed and
redacted paths are listed in `DATA_EXCLUSIONS.md`.

The source code is released under the MIT license (see `LICENSE`). **The
derived aggregate results are not MIT-licensed.** They remain subject to the
ICEWS research-and-teaching terms and are provided only for research and
teaching. Redistribution outside those terms is not permitted. Cite ICEWS v37
(doi:10.7910/DVN/28075) alongside this artifact.

No other third-party dataset (for example UNGA votes, ideal points or Wikidata)
is used by the public paper path or included in this release.
